<p>Greek police arrested an 89-year-old man after shootings at a social security office and a courthouse in central Athens wounded five people Tuesday, Greek authorities and state broadcaster ERT said. The suspect first opened fire with a shotgun at an EFKA social security office in the Kerameikos area, wounding an employee in the leg, before a second shooting at a court building injured four more people, authorities said. ERT said the injuries were not life-threatening. The suspect fled after the shootings and was detained hours later in the western port city of Patras, about 200 to 210 kilometers from Athens, according to police and Greek media. Several reports linked the case to a pension dispute, but authorities had not announced a formal motive; ERT said the man reportedly left envelopes with documents at the courthouse and said they explained his actions.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/gIi63Wl6c3Esm_UOOFTf80Uz4yV-UcEXHKrS5wQZQH1PV6Ff8Z1S5XxYmcQ4iWDQoqQaYb32EaK0SXqlpmo1nIaF5f3yAGueDhpBhI5c4_Otgu0CoYP7rXNnlcv9fAuF_d7dHp9wce_Pj9MTZx2iCqLct1fR-BA3OV2u6ruwa9OWXGvG9I1ULYrwAHlckBMWh0sWOKl5ICSvEfcAQolnh3fbel5mWYssDaSYwlQTCKDFzSECZ8E5s6MI4nCAkEQlirev8zkzOprTi4-8GJ5sWxlatFhq' alt='Emergency response near the Athens courthouse after the shooting.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Camera footage: Security camera footage aired by Greek media showed a man walking calmly near the social security office carrying what appeared to be a short-barrelled shotgun.</li><li>Weapon recovered: The shotgun was later recovered at the courthouse, police said.</li><li>Between locations: Intellinews said the suspect travelled by taxi from the EFKA office to the Athens Court of Appeals before the second shooting.</li><li>Mental-health reports: Some reports said the suspect had psychological issues or had previously spent time in a psychiatric facility.</li></ul><blockquote>He went in, went up to the fourth floor, raised his shotgun, told an employee to duck and hit another one - A